MCP — Notes from Our Playwright + Nemotron Setup
1. What is MCP?

MCP = Model Context Protocol

MCP is a standard way for an AI model to communicate with external tools and systems.

Simple idea:

LLM
 ↓
MCP Client
 ↓
MCP Server
 ↓
External Tool

For our case:

Nemotron
   ↓
MCP Client
   ↓
Playwright MCP
   ↓
Playwright
   ↓
Browser
2. MCP Server vs MCP Client
MCP Server

Provides tools to the AI.

In our case:

Playwright MCP

It provides browser tools such as:

browser_navigate
browser_snapshot
browser_click
browser_type
browser_fill_form
browser_tabs
browser_take_screenshot
...
MCP Client

Connects to the MCP server and calls those tools.

We created our own Python MCP client using the MCP Python SDK.

3. What we installed
Node.js

We checked:

node --version

Result:

v24.19.0

This is suitable for Playwright MCP.

Playwright MCP

Initially:

npx @playwright/mcp@latest

was taking too long.

We tested npm:

npm ping

Result:

PONG 323ms

Then:

npm view @playwright/mcp version

Result:

0.0.80

So npm connectivity was working.

Instead of npx, we installed it globally:

npm install -g @playwright/mcp

Installation succeeded.

4. Verify Playwright MCP

We ran:

playwright-mcp --help

This confirmed that the Playwright MCP server was installed.

5. Python MCP SDK

Inside our Python .venv, we installed:

pip install "mcp[cli]"

and:

pip install openai python-dotenv

Purpose:

mcp
    → communicate with MCP servers

openai
    → communicate with OpenRouter's OpenAI-compatible API

python-dotenv
    → read API key from .env
6. Our first MCP Client

We created:

Next/
│
├── mcp_test/
│   └── mcp_client.py
│
└── RS/
    └── Playwright_23AUG/

The client connects to:

StdioServerParameters(
    command="playwright-mcp",
    args=[]
)

Then:

await session.initialize()

initializes the MCP connection.

Then:

response = await session.list_tools()

retrieves the tools provided by Playwright MCP.

We successfully received:

browser_navigate
browser_snapshot
browser_click
browser_type
browser_find
browser_tabs
browser_take_screenshot
...

This proved:

Python
  ↓
MCP Client
  ↓
Playwright MCP

was working.

7. We then connected Nemotron

Our model is:

nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free

through:

OpenRouter

Our architecture became:

                    ┌───────────────────┐
                    │ Nemotron 3 Ultra  │
                    └─────────┬─────────┘
                              │
                         OpenRouter
                              │
                              ▼
                    ┌───────────────────┐
                    │ Python MCP Client │
                    └─────────┬─────────┘
                              │
                         MCP Protocol
                              │
                              ▼
                    ┌───────────────────┐
                    │  Playwright MCP   │
                    └─────────┬─────────┘
                              │
                              ▼
                           Browser
8. What is Tool Calling here?

Nemotron doesn't directly control Chrome.

Instead, Nemotron decides:

Which tool should I use?

For example:

browser_navigate

or:

browser_click

or:

browser_snapshot

Our Python MCP client receives that decision and calls the corresponding MCP tool.

So:

Nemotron
   ↓
"I want browser_click"
   ↓
MCP Client
   ↓
Playwright MCP
   ↓
Browser click
9. Our Successful Test

We gave Nemotron this task:

Open https://rahulshettyacademy.com/loginpagePractise/
and click the blinking text link.

Nemotron dynamically performed:

browser_navigate
        ↓
browser_snapshot
        ↓
browser_find
        ↓
browser_click
        ↓
browser_tabs
        ↓
browser_tabs

It found:

Free Access to InterviewQues/ResumeAssistance/Material link

and clicked it.

The link opened a new tab:

https://rahulshettyacademy.com/documents-request

Nemotron recognized the new tab and selected it.

This confirms that our complete MCP + LLM + browser flow is working.

10. Traditional Playwright vs MCP
Traditional Playwright

We write the exact automation:

page.goto(url)

page.locator(".blinkingText").first.click()

We decide:

URL
Locator
Index
Action
MCP + AI

We give the AI an objective:

Open the website and click the blinking text.

Nemotron decides:

Navigate
   ↓
Inspect page
   ↓
Find element
   ↓
Click element

So:

Traditional:
Human → writes automation → Playwright → Browser

MCP:
Human → gives objective → AI → MCP → Playwright → Browser
11. Our Existing Playwright Framework

We deliberately did not modify your existing framework yet.

Your existing project is:

RS/
└── Playwright_23AUG/
    ├── data/
    ├── pageObjects/
    ├── pytest/
    ├── utils/
    ├── conftest.py
    ├── test_*.py
    └── ...

We kept MCP separately:

Next/
├── mcp_test/
│   ├── mcp_client.py
│   └── nemotron_playwright.py
│
└── RS/
    └── Playwright_23AUG/
        └── existing framework

This is good for learning because we aren't mixing:

pytest
Playwright
Page Objects
MCP
Agents
LLM

all at once.

12. Important Concept to Remember

MCP itself is not an AI model.

Nemotron = LLM / Brain
MCP = Standard communication protocol
Playwright MCP = MCP server providing browser tools
Playwright = Browser automation technology
Chrome = Browser

Think of it like:

             BRAIN
            Nemotron
               │
               │ "click this"
               ▼
          MCP CLIENT
               │
               │ MCP
               ▼
        PLAYWRIGHT MCP
               │
               ▼
          PLAYWRIGHT
               │
               ▼
            CHROME
